    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535">

                <pb facs="0696" n="576" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg576"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Griscom.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-11-04"><hi rendition="#italic">November 4,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 84.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith for your information
                    copies of a letter and its accompanying inclosure from the Department of the
                    Interior, also of the Department’s reply thereto, in relation to the destruction
                    of sea fowl on Midway and other islands of the Hawaiian group by Japanese
                    subjects.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. B. Loomis.</hi></signed></closer>





